1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,509
Welcome to Module eight,
all about marketing!

2
00:00:03,509 --> 00:00:06,318
In this lesson, you'll design a beautiful,

3
00:00:06,318 --> 00:00:09,528
branded email in Kyntlo's
drag and drop builder.

4
00:00:09,528 --> 00:00:11,735
No code, no design skills needed.

5
00:00:12,599 --> 00:00:16,056
Email campaigns live under
Marketing, in the Emails tab.

6
00:00:16,056 --> 00:00:20,315
Here you can see every campaign
you've created, whether it's a draft,

7
00:00:20,315 --> 00:00:25,006
scheduled or already sent, along with
how many people opened and clicked it.

8
00:00:25,855 --> 00:00:28,407
To create a new one, click New campaign.

9
00:00:28,407 --> 00:00:31,981
You can start from a blank
canvas, a pre-built template,

10
00:00:31,981 --> 00:00:34,214
or one of your own saved templates.

11
00:00:34,214 --> 00:00:36,703
Saved templates are the secret to fast,

12
00:00:36,703 --> 00:00:41,106
consistent emails: build your branding
once, and reuse it every time.

13
00:00:41,956 --> 00:00:43,587
Let's pick the event invite.

14
00:00:43,587 --> 00:00:45,219
The builder has three parts.

15
00:00:45,219 --> 00:00:47,608
On the left are the elements you can add.

16
00:00:47,608 --> 00:00:51,046
In the middle is your email,
exactly as people will see it.

17
00:00:51,046 --> 00:00:54,833
And on the right are the settings
for whatever you've clicked on.

18
00:00:55,682 --> 00:00:58,668
First, give your campaign
a clear name at the top.

19
00:00:58,668 --> 00:01:02,311
Only your team sees this name,
so make it easy to find later,

20
00:01:02,311 --> 00:01:04,043
like the event and the month.

21
00:01:04,893 --> 00:01:07,067
Now click the heading to edit it.

22
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:09,175
Let's greet each person by name.

23
00:01:09,175 --> 00:01:12,733
Type Hi, then open Merge
fields and choose First name.

24
00:01:12,733 --> 00:01:17,872
When the email goes out, Kyntlo swaps
that placeholder for each contact's real

25
00:01:17,872 --> 00:01:18,597
first name.

26
00:01:19,447 --> 00:01:20,510
Next, the button.

27
00:01:20,510 --> 00:01:25,262
Click it, and change the text to something
specific about what happens next.

28
00:01:25,262 --> 00:01:27,950
Below that is the
website address it opens.

29
00:01:27,950 --> 00:01:32,265
A clear button is the single biggest
thing that gets people to click.

30
00:01:33,114 --> 00:01:37,295
To add something new, drag an element
from the left onto your email.

31
00:01:37,295 --> 00:01:40,061
Let's drop in a video,
just under the button.

32
00:01:40,061 --> 00:01:42,828
Email apps can't play
video inside the email,

33
00:01:42,828 --> 00:01:47,070
so Kyntlo shows a thumbnail with a
play button that opens your video.

34
00:01:47,921 --> 00:01:52,654
Most people will read your email on their
phone, so always check the mobile view.

35
00:01:52,654 --> 00:01:54,056
Click Mobile at the top.

36
00:01:54,056 --> 00:01:56,451
Everything stacks neatly into one column,

37
00:01:56,451 --> 00:01:59,665
and the button is still big
enough to tap with a thumb.

38
00:02:00,519 --> 00:02:04,080
Before any real customer sees
it, send a test to yourself.

39
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:06,597
Click Send test email, check the address,

40
00:02:06,597 --> 00:02:09,482
and pick a contact to
fill in the merge fields.

41
00:02:09,482 --> 00:02:12,674
Then open it on your own
phone and click every link.

42
00:02:13,525 --> 00:02:14,422
Happy with it?

43
00:02:14,422 --> 00:02:15,127
Click Save.

44
00:02:15,127 --> 00:02:19,421
Your campaign is stored as a draft,
ready to send whenever you are.

45
00:02:19,421 --> 00:02:23,971
If you'll reuse this design, open
the menu and choose Save as template.

46
00:02:23,971 --> 00:02:27,111
Next month's email then
takes minutes, not hours.

47
00:02:27,961 --> 00:02:29,013
Here's a pro tip.

48
00:02:29,013 --> 00:02:31,922
Give every email one
goal, and one main button.

49
00:02:31,922 --> 00:02:36,440
When you offer five different things,
people usually choose none of them.

50
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:38,669
Keep it short, friendly and focused.

51
00:02:39,518 --> 00:02:40,180
Great work!

52
00:02:40,180 --> 00:02:42,647
You've designed your first branded email.

53
00:02:42,647 --> 00:02:46,378
In the next lesson, we'll choose
who receives it, schedule it,

54
00:02:46,378 --> 00:02:47,822
and see how it performs.

55
00:02:47,822 --> 00:02:48,665
See you there.
